          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "The September work order is **WO-2025-09-004 (MO-25-09-1070)** at Modine’s Racine operation. Its component-issue event **CE-250904-0004** references source transaction **TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070**.\n\n- **Amount:** 28,476,342 cents ($284,763.42)\n- **Event created:** 2025-09-30T19:15:00\n- **September period entered Pending Close:** 2025-09-30T18:00:00\n- **Lateness:** 75 minutes\n- **Recorded accounting status:** POSTED\n\n**Conclusion: The recorded status is not consistent with the documented Pending Close treatment.** Oracle’s 26B guidance says newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged for Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting, and are processed after the period is closed or reopened. This was a newly created INPUT transaction, not one of the stated exceptions.\n\nThe review was read-only; no database records were changed.",
